        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pepper Keenan, Rob Parissi\n- Roles: guitarist, vocalist, singer, songwriter, frontman\n- Organizations: Corrosion of Conformity, Down, Wild Cherry\n- Places: Mingo Junction, Ohio\n- Works: Play That Funky Music\n\nFacts:\n- Rob Parissi was born in 1950 and was raised in the steel mill town of Mingo Junction, Ohio.\n- Pepper J. Keenan was born on May 8, 1967, and is an American guitarist and vocalist.\n- Rob Parissi is an American singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Pepper Keenan is best known for his work with the heavy metal bands Corrosion of Conformity and Down.\n- Rob Parissi is best known as the frontman of the American funk group Wild Cherry.\n- Wild Cherry is best known for the 1976 chart-topping song \"Play That Funky Music,\" which Rob Parissi wrote.",
